"tool": "open_pr", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-money-round-half-even", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 375392, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01WhjiQTT894ZfbyCjednGju", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 379929, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I fixed the rounding bug, CI passed, and I opened PR #101 against main with alex as reviewer.\n\n- **Cause:** `round_money` in `src/money.py` used `ROUND_HALF_UP`, even though its docstring says it uses banker's rounding (`ROUND_HALF_EVEN`, per FIN-212). That's why the 2.665 \u2192 2.66 case in `tests/test_money.py` failed.\n- **Fix:** On the new branch `fix/money-round-half-even`, I changed that function to use `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`. Nothing else changed.\n- **CI:** Run ci-0001 passed on commit 08d3cd5986.\n- **PR:** #101 is at https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101. It's not merged; merging into main needs a code owner's approval.\n\nWhen I looked up FIN-212 in the advisory system, it came back as unknown. I made the change based on what the test and docstring say, so it's worth checking that FIN-212 really calls for banker's rounding.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01J17yBdx2vZJRyFQXEXp6p7", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "src/money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01P4b4ZAHfDucj99FuXKPqTp", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "tests/test_money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_018jdc7gYWdjb65p4SECPCxY", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"id": "FIN-212"}, "name": "get_advisory", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_018FG6hsZsenmEbhs77AXu7C", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/money-round-half-even"}, "name": "create_branch", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01JzRagUYYYFhz7ouc2DCSuL", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/money-round-half-even", "message": "Use banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN) in round_money per FIN-212", "files": [{"path": "src/money.py", "content": "from decimal import Decimal, ROUND_HALF_EVEN\n\n\ndef round_money(amount: Decimal) -> Decimal:\n    \"\"\"Round to cents using banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN), per FIN-212.\"\"\"\n    return amount.quantize(Decimal(\"0.01\"), rounding=ROUND_HALF_EVEN)\n"}]}, "name": "commit_changes", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01UHA5ghwfdytTujAQwfXNYk", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"ref": "fix/money-round-half-even", "idempotency_key": "ci-fix-money-round-half-even-08d3cd5986"}, "name": "trigger_ci", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01LiBop4unXifAMPKGAjWvAi", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"run_id": "ci-0001"}, "name": "wait_for_ci", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01WhjiQTT894ZfbyCjednGju", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"head": "fix/money-round-half-even", "base": "main", "title": "Fix round_money to use banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN)", "body": "The nightly build was failing because `tests/test_money.py::test_half_even` expects banker's rounding (per FIN-212), but `src/money.py` used `ROUND_HALF_UP` even though its docstring said ROUND_HALF_EVEN.\n\nThis change switches `round_money` to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`. Now 2.675 rounds to 2.68 and 2.665 rounds to 2.66.\n\nCI: ci-0001 passed on 08d3cd5986.", "reviewers": ["alex"], "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-money-round-half-even"}, "name": "open_pr", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I fixed the rounding bug, CI passed, and I opened PR #101 against main with alex as reviewer.\n\n- **Cause:** `round_money` in `src/money.py` used `ROUND_HALF_UP`, even though its docstring says it uses banker's rounding (`ROUND_HALF_EVEN`, per FIN-212). That's why the 2.665 \u2192 2.66 case in `tests/test_money.py` failed.\n- **Fix:** On the new branch `fix/money-round-half-even`, I changed that function to use `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`. Nothing else changed.\n- **CI:** Run ci-0001 passed on commit 08d3cd5986.\n- **PR:** #101 is at https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101. It's not merged; merging into main needs a code owner's approval.\n\nWhen I looked up FIN-212 in the advisory system, it came back as unknown. I made the change based on what the test and docstring say, so it's worth checking that FIN-212 really calls for banker's rounding.", "type": "text"}]}]}